Dragon scale mail is seldom a bad use of a
wish, assuming you don't already have some.
You made a good choice.  I can't say for sure
that it was the absolute best of all possible
choices, but it was definitely a good choice.
Wearing DSM not only improves your AC by
quite a bit and thus your survivability; it also
significantly reduces the amount of weight
your armor imposes, allowing you to carry
more.  Oh, and it doesn't impede casting like
metal body armor does.  It's just an all-around
great thing to have.

The choice of silver versus gray will depend
somewhat on how you plan to obtain magic
resistance.  Either is great, of course; it's
just a question of which is the very best...

For neutral characters, I definitely prefer silver
DSM, because in all probability you won't see
too many artifacts before the castle and will be
able to wish then for The Eye of the Aethiopica
(or some other MR-granting artifact; neutrals
have a couple of good ones to choose from),
leaving the amulet slot open for live-saving
and the cloak slot for a robe, without requiring
you to keep a shield of reflection on at all times.

For characters who never plan to cast any
spells, the robe is of less value and a cloak
of magic resistance becomes an option, which
again makes silver DSM the better choice.

But I can definitely see a lawful or chaotic
character choosing gray DSM if they feel they
will want to wear a robe later.


